WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.329 --> 00:00:04.410
Whether he's playing a Jedi or the director
of S.H.I.E.L.D., Samuel L. Jackson always

00:00:04.410 --> 00:00:05.480
follows his instincts.

00:00:05.720 --> 00:00:07.520
And those instincts are often funny.

00:00:07.580 --> 00:00:09.100
"We're going to seal off this…"

00:00:11.720 --> 00:00:14.460
Sometimes, though, his jokes aren't entirely
on purpose.

00:00:14.600 --> 00:00:18.780
That leads to some outrageous bloopers and
outtakes, both for himself and his co-stars.

00:00:19.160 --> 00:00:21.100
Here are some times when he cut loose.

00:00:21.720 --> 00:00:24.100
Nick Fury is a serious, serious man.

00:00:24.120 --> 00:00:26.260
Samuel L. Jackson, you know…not so much.

00:00:26.600 --> 00:00:30.390
But the guy is such a professional, he manages
to keep it serious even when everyone else

00:00:30.390 --> 00:00:31.660
around him is screwing up.

00:00:32.200 --> 00:00:33.820
"Why am I going over here?"

00:00:33.830 --> 00:00:36.310
"Because, see him on the thing and tell him,
you know…"

00:00:36.310 --> 00:00:37.310
"But why did I do that?"

00:00:37.310 --> 00:00:39.340
"...and don't be going all stealth mode, motherf--er,
we can't see you."

00:00:40.360 --> 00:00:45.360
The 2017 action flick The Hitman's Bodyguard
gave fans the chance to see Deadpool and Nick

00:00:45.360 --> 00:00:46.900
Fury together at last.

00:00:47.060 --> 00:00:48.840
Well, at least the actors who played them.

00:00:49.340 --> 00:00:52.140
So it's no surprise there were a lot of casualties
in the film.

00:00:52.360 --> 00:00:56.900
What's a surprise is there were some casualties
behind the scenes as well, such as this poor

00:00:56.900 --> 00:00:57.400
dude.

00:01:00.820 --> 00:01:01.820
"Oh, s---!"

00:01:02.780 --> 00:01:03.280
"Cut it!"

00:01:04.920 --> 00:01:05.960
Poor Mace Windu.

00:01:06.200 --> 00:01:09.600
He should have been the ultimate hero, but
instead he got blown out a window thanks to

00:01:09.600 --> 00:01:10.760
Anakin's betrayal.

00:01:11.160 --> 00:01:14.700
At least Jackson was able to have some fun
with it though, filming it over and over again

00:01:14.710 --> 00:01:19.030
while pretending the safety mat was a big
comfy mattress, and his death was just a bad

00:01:19.030 --> 00:01:19.520
dream.

00:01:21.200 --> 00:01:22.960
"Oh my god, I'm awake!

00:01:24.100 --> 00:01:24.600
It's morning!"

00:01:25.280 --> 00:01:29.440
Even though he's known for playing a guy with
one eye, Jackson seems to have amazing peripheral

00:01:29.450 --> 00:01:33.820
vision or something, because in this blooper
from xXx: The Return of Xander Cage, he seems

00:01:33.820 --> 00:01:35.760
to know exactly what's happening behind him!

00:01:36.060 --> 00:01:39.460
"Because soldiers are built to take orders
and fight wars.

00:01:40.020 --> 00:01:43.740
But we my friend, are not at war.

00:01:44.520 --> 00:01:45.620
They're at war behind us!"

00:01:46.460 --> 00:01:51.380
It can't be easy for Maria Hill, the deputy
director of SHIELD under taskmaster Nick Fury.

00:01:51.660 --> 00:01:56.440
And it can't be easy for actress Cobie Smulders
either, as, like Fury himself, Jackson is

00:01:56.440 --> 00:01:59.250
always watching and ready to pounce on any
screw up.

00:01:59.660 --> 00:02:02.300
"I got confused with my eye line, I think
I looked directly into camera."

00:02:02.300 --> 00:02:03.120
"I don't care.

00:02:03.300 --> 00:02:05.560
You just forgot the line, now you're trying
to make up other s---."

00:02:06.360 --> 00:02:11.160
In the 2003 action flick S.W.A.T., Jackson
plays a Los Angeles Police Department sergeant

00:02:11.160 --> 00:02:13.280
tasked with putting together an elite force.

00:02:13.560 --> 00:02:15.680
But only if he can keep his balance first!

00:02:16.040 --> 00:02:18.220
"I heard some rumors about you and your old
partner."

00:02:22.120 --> 00:02:26.720
Just like in S.W.A.T., Samuel L. Jackson plays
a tough as nails cop in the 2010 comedy The

00:02:26.720 --> 00:02:27.420
Other Guys.

00:02:27.660 --> 00:02:32.200
And like in S.W.A.T., gravity is his downfall,
that and the fact that co-star Dwayne "The

00:02:32.209 --> 00:02:35.030
Rock" Johnson seems to have no idea what Jackson
is doing.

00:02:35.030 --> 00:02:35.600
Whoops!

00:02:36.020 --> 00:02:38.200
"Tuck and roll when you're hit!

00:02:38.900 --> 00:02:40.280
AAAAH!"

00:02:40.920 --> 00:02:41.420
"...oops."

00:02:41.720 --> 00:02:44.540
"I didn't know if we're supposed to go!"

